WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.510
For his novels' countryside, Thomas Hardy
borrowed a name from an extinct kingdom:

2
00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:06.590
Wessex.

3
00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:10.270
He called it a merely
realistic dream-country.

4
00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.750
By 1895, the press and
public had taken up the name.

5
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:16.950
The dream still pulls.

6
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:22.450
In the year to June 2023, more people
moved into England's mostly rural council

7
00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:24.350
areas than moved out.

8
00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:27.230
So why do some people dream
of moving to a village,

9
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:30.350
while teenagers can't wait to leave?

10
00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:34.190
In this mission, you'll weigh
the rural idyll against data,

11
00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:36.430
lived experience and the media.

12
00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.250
Then you'll map rural
England as a spectrum,

13
00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:43.490
from very remote areas to
retirement and commuter villages.

14
00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:48.570
Your mission: explain why the same
countryside draws some people in and pushes

15
00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:49.710
others out.
